import-review's review file with the router up (host.pid.self): `server import
--apply` rewrites the pool, lists it (`after_import`) and reloads. The sandbox's
sing-box exits at once, so the restart does not come back: the listing is on
stdout, then no-limbo's proxy line — and the exit status is 0, because
`apply_import` goes on to say how many domains the escape lane has and the arm
then `return 0`s. (`server rm`, by contrast, ends in the reload: see
pool-seeded-running.)
